From d3794c203339fb9e2046f834ba1a726c9ba0c496 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:28:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Bound review author exclusions to the current
 implementation epoch

Why: every implementation run accumulated forever on long-churn cards, so
four review/rework cycles could exclude every independent reviewer. The
reviewer resolver then requeued an impossible spawn instead of stopping.

Keep all concrete authors after the last real review preceding the latest
implementation; keep the epoch across review-only retries, failed spawns,
and unknown current receipts. Retain first-epoch pin provenance and source
card traversal. Structural exhaustion now has a typed refusal propagated
through model-tier dispatch into the canonical sticky infrastructure triage
block, with named excluded models, rather than a spawn-failure retry loop.
Temporary provider walls retain bounded infrastructure deferrals.

Proof: six new acceptance cases RED on b28fa0fa569f; 10 epoch/exhaustion
regressions GREEN. 40 consumer files: 1089 passed, 0 failed. Seven source
mutants killed using the canonical runner. scripts/check: 21 checks pass.
Read-only replay of local boards and full replicas: 994 same-card histories,
31 changed author sets, each requiring a real review boundary. Replay found
unknown-receipt histories; conservative retention was added and tested.
Independent exact-head review and required green CI remain ship gates.
